===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|quene}}, {{m|enm|queen}}, {{m|enm|cwen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cwēn||queen}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kwāni}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kwēniz||woman}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʷḗn|*gʷénh₂s|woman}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|queen}}, {{m|sco|wheen||queen}}, {{cog|osx|quān}} {{gloss|"wife"; > {{cog|gml|-}} {{m|gml|quene||elderly woman}}}}, {{cog|nl|kween||woman past child-bearing age}}, {{cog|sv|kvinna||woman}}, {{cog|no|kvinne||woman}}, {{cog|da|kvinde||woman}}, {{cog|is|kvon||wife}}, {{cog|got|𐌵𐌴𐌽𐍃||wife}}, {{cog|no|-}} dialectal {{m|no|kvån||wife}}. Related to and possibly merged with and/or absorbed some senses of {{m+|en|quean}}, from {{cog|enm|quene}}, from {{cog|ang|cwene|t=woman; female serf, quean}}, see {{l|en|quean}}. Generally eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|regina|t=queen}}, borrowed from {{noncog|la|rēgīna|t=queen}} (see Modern English {{m|en|regina}}). {{doublet|en|quean|gyne}}.

