===Verb===
{{en-verb}}
[[File:Chess queen 0964.jpg|thumb|upright|A white queen (''n., {{senseno|en|chess piece}}'') on a {{l|en|chessboard}}]]

# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To act the part of a queen; to behave {{l|en|imperiously}}; to [[queen it]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make a [[#Noun|queen]] or (''figuratively'') to give the status of a queen.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|IV|iv|295|1|This dreame of mine / Being now awake, Ile '''Queene''' it no inch farther, / But milke my Ewes, and weepe.}}
# {{lb|en|chess}} To [[promote]] a [[pawn]] to a [[#English: chess piece|queen]].
#* {{quote-book|en|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books?id=7pPaDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA39-IA1|title=Winning Chess Endings|author=w:Yasser Seirawan|publisher=Everyman Chess|location=London|isbn=9781857443486|year=2003|page=39|passage=Neither King will be able to stop the opponent's pawns from '''queening''', when the game should be a draw. In such cases, which side '''queens''' first, or '''queens''' with check, can make a crucial difference. In this case, White promotes his pawn first and is able to put this advantage to good use.}}
# {{lb|en|beekeeping}} To be the queen bee of a colony.
#* {{quote-journal |en |date=22 November 1882 |author=E.&nbsp;L. Briggs |title=Development of ‘The Coming Bee’ |url=https://archive.org/details/sim_american-bee-journal_1882-11-22_18_47 |journal=The American Bee Journal |volume=18 |issue=47 |page=743 |accessdate=15 January 2022 |passage=They have all been '''queened''' by imported stock, or the best of home-bred mothers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|title=The Wealth of India|author=Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (India)|page=263|ISBN=|passage=The nucleus should not be '''queened''' by a queen from any of the parent colonies.}}
# {{lb|en|beekeeping}} To provide with a new queen bee.
#: {{antonyms|en|dequeen}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1896|title=The Progressive Bee-Keeper|author=|page=320|ISBN=|passage=In '''queening''' his apiary, he aims to keep about half of the queens of the current season's rearing, and the other of the summer preceding.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1967|title=Are Bees Reflex Machines?|author=Everett Franklin Phillips|page=|ISBN=|passage=If such a queen is immediately allowed to run through the entrance of a queenless colony, the '''queening''' is usually successful.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|title=Hunting Wild Bees|author=Robert E. Donovan|page=|ISBN=|passage=Once you have introduced the queen, the first three steps of the capture have been completed, namely: blocking the tree, providing an alternate home, and '''queening''' the colony.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=The Complete Book on Beekeeping and Honey Processing|author=NPCS Board of Consultants & Engineers|page=389|ISBN=8190568558|passage=Sealed cells with about to emerge queens are used for '''queening''' the divisions.}}
# {{lb|en|BDSM|slang|transitive|usually|of a woman}} To sit on a person’s face to receive [[oral sex]], typically while [[straddling]] the person’s head.
#: {{synonyms|en|face-sit|king}}
#* {{quote-book |en |year=1996 |author=Lorelei |title=The Mistress Manual: The Good Girl’s Guide to Female Dominance |location=Scranton, Pennsylvania |publisher=Berkana Press |isbn=978-0-9648561-0-3 |page=138 |passage=The classic posture, in which you lie on your back while the male serves you, may make him feel arrogant and in charge. Try '''Queening''' him. Have him lie on his back while you sit on his face (make sure he has an airway through either his mouth or his nose).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Yolanda Celbridge|title=The Castle of Maldona|passage=She saw his pink tongue flickering on Clare's exposed nympha as she '''queened''' him, her love juices shining on his chin and throat{{...}}}}

